sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (Nick approved 2026-11-07): one VM bakes the next image and seed; idle slots then re-enroll from it with their fixed identities. Replaces the full task VM provision, Save the ready copies, the builder VM, the smoke VM and the check VM.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: none · after a release, and daily
  %% kind: task_vm.image_refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=refresh VM tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Refresh VM<br/>current image
  Note over GW: Admit the refresh<br/>one run per host
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - the release projection, when the release changed playbooks, pins or lock files; a daily schedule
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the intent holds the release commit, the current image and the host; a second admission returns the open run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-image-refresh
  SW->>H: Start the refresh VM<br/>from the current image
  SW->>VM: Converge everything<br/>one Ansible run
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - outer VM: packages, tools, Swamp, orbit-agent, the Pi server, sshd and UFW at the release's pins
  %%> - the warm checkout: main at the release commit, with `vendor/` and `node_modules/`
  %%> - each container: its role phases, the checkout device, migrations, services running; cloud-init off
  %%> - then a new `base` snapshot of each container
  SW->>H: Publish the image<br/>under the host lock
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the refresh VM, publishes it as the candidate image and snapshots its container disk as the candidate's seed; the refresh VM is deleted
  SW->>H: Re-enroll one slot<br/>proves the candidate
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - rebuilds the first idle slot from the candidate with its fixed identity (`task_vm.slot_enroll`), takes its `clean` snapshot, then runs the claim's ready check
  %%> Why: this replaces the smoke VM and the check VM; it proves exactly what a claim gets
  SW->>H: Promote<br/>keep -previous
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the alias moves to the candidate, the old image keeps `-previous` for rollback, and older images are removed
  %%> - the other idle slots re-enroll one at a time; a claimed slot re-enrolls when it is released
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>new image
    Note over GW: Record the image<br/>target about 3 min
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the host keeps its image; the refresh VM and the candidate are removed, and the slot re-enrolls from the current image
  end
